# .gitattributes — Unity project
#
# Purpose: stop Git from applying line-ending (CRLF<->LF) conversion to Unity's
# binary asset files. Without this, a clone/download on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true can silently corrupt binary .asset files (e.g. TerrainData),
# which makes the terrain / scene fail to load with console errors.
#
# `-text` marks a pattern as binary: Git stores and checks it out byte-for-byte,
# on every machine, regardless of that machine's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Normal source/text files are left to auto-normalization.
* text=auto

## ---- Unity serialized assets (THE FIX for corrupted terrain / .asset on clone) ----
*.asset              -text
*.unity              -text
*.prefab             -text
*.mat                -text
*.anim               -text
*.controller         -text
